UPDATE companies SET description='Universal Solar, LLC is based in Millersburg, Pennsylvania. The company has been operating for nearly a decade, though a specific founding year is not disclosed. It began as a response to unstable electricity in rural areas, aiming to provide energy-efficient solutions for properties in the region.

The company provides solar energy system design, installation, repair, and maintenance. Services include off-grid solar systems, grid-tied systems, grid-interactive systems, roof-mounted and ground-mount solar panel installations, battery storage solutions, and solar water pumping (Simple Pump). They serve residential, commercial, and industrial clients. No facility size, headcount, or volume metrics are published.

Universal Solar serves homeowners, businesses, and industrial facilities across central and northeastern Pennsylvania, including Millersburg, Bloomsburg, Lewisburg, Williamsport, Scranton, and Wilkes-Barre. Customers range from residential property owners seeking backup power to commercial and industrial operations looking to lower energy costs.

The company emphasizes energy independence and reliability during grid outages, positioning its installations as a way to avoid peak-rate charges and reduce environmental impact. Financing options are offered to lower the upfront investment barrier.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Off-grid solar system design and installation", "Grid-tied solar system installation", "Grid-interactive system installation", "Solar panel installation and repair", "Roof-mounted solar panel installation", "Ground-mount solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Industrial solar power installation", "Battery storage solutions", "Solar system maintenance and inspection", "Solar water pumping (Simple Pump)"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Agricultural"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Company name: Universal Solar, LLC -> db", "Headquarters: Millersburg, PA -> db", "Services: off-grid, grid-tied, grid-interactive solar systems, solar panel installation/repair, battery storage, solar water pumping -> /", "Service area: Millersburg, Bloomsburg, Lewisburg, Williamsport, Scranton, Wilkes-Barre, and other PA towns -> /", "Owner/technician: Elmer -> /", "Financing options available -> /", "Focus on energy independence and grid vulnerability -> /", "Nearly a decade of experience -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Our services include: Off solar grid system, Grid-tied solar system, Interactive grid, Solar panel installation, Well pump", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='universal-solar-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Uptown Millworks operates from its workshop in New Orleans, Louisiana. Founded by Christian Pokorn, a woodworker from a multi-generational Austrian sawmill family who also leads Pokorn Construction, the shop began as a locally owned and operated custom millwork business dedicated to the architectural heritage of its home city.

The company produces architectural millwork, casework, and furniture using time-tested woodworking techniques alongside modern precision tools. Services span handrails, flooring, cypress slabs, custom cabinets, moldings, windows, doors, shutters, and turnings. A team of millwrights, carpenters, and woodworkers executes each project from the New Orleans facility, sourcing, manufacturing, and finishing all work on-site without maintaining large inventory.

Uptown Millworks serves residential, hospitality, and commercial clients across Louisiana, including historic homes, restaurants, hotels, and upscale buildings in the greater New Orleans area. The shop frequently collaborates on historically faithful restorations guided by the New Orleans Historic District Landmarks Commission.

The firm distinguishes itself through a commitment to local manufacturing, sustainable material sourcing (FSC-certified woods), and adherence to Architectural Woodwork Institute standards. Waste is minimized by repurposing offcuts for smaller details or donating to community gardens and shelters, and every piece is delivered and installed by the company''s own crew.', certifications=ARRAY['Architectural Woodwork Institute (AWI) standards','Forest Stewardship Council (FSC) certified materials','New Orleans Historic District Landmarks Commission regulations']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Architectural millwork", "Casework", "Custom cabinets", "Custom furniture", "Handrails", "Flooring", "Cypress slabs", "Moldings and millwork", "Windows, doors, and shutters", "Turnings", "Custom projects", "Historic restoration", "Woodworking (time-tested techniques)", "Precision machining (modern tools)"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Hospitality (restaurants, hotels)", "Commercial construction", "Historic preservation", "Architectural millwork"], "materials": ["Cypress", "FSC-certified hardwoods", "Locally sourced lumber", "Natural woods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All work sourced, manufactured, and finished in New Orleans", "Adherence to AWI, FSC, and NOLA Historic District Landmarks Commission standards", "Custom historic preservation and restoration expertise", "Sustainable practices: FSC-certified woods, minimal waste, recycling of offcuts", "Experienced team of millwrights, carpenters, and woodworkers with over ten years on upscale projects"], "facts_used": ["Located in New Orleans, Louisiana -> db", "Founded by Christian Pokorn -> /about-us", "Christian Pokorn comes from a long line of woodworkers in Austria and is principal of Pokorn Construction -> /about-us", "Services: Handrails, Flooring, Cypress Slabs, Custom projects, Moldings and millwork, Windows, doors and shutters, Custom cabinets, Turnings -> /services", "All work sourced, manufactured, and finished in New Orleans -> /", "Adheres to AWI, FSC, and NOLA Historic District Landmarks Commission standards -> /quality", "Sustainable practices: FSC-certified woods, minimal waste, recycling offcuts -> /quality", "Serves Louisiana houses, restaurants, hotels, commercial spaces -> /", "Team of millwrights, carpenters, woodworkers with over ten years experience -> /about-us", "Locally owned and operated -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Uptown Millworks is a New Orleans millwork shop and furniture maker specializing in quality, style and function.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='uptown-millworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Urth Apparel Inc. is a custom apparel manufacturer headquartered in Newport Beach, California. The company was founded in 2013 when its founder launched an international trade cooperative focused on natural foods and cotton apparel from Peru. The venture grew from a desire to find manufacturing partners that shared a commitment to both fashionable design and ecological responsibility.

Urth Apparel manages the full product development cycle, including fashion and technical design, fabric and trim sourcing, pattern making, grading, marker making, sampling, cutting and sewing, screen printing, sublimation, heat transfer, finishing, packaging, and inspection. Production is distributed across three origins: luxury clothing in Italy, knitwear and basics in Peru, and specialty technical apparel in the United States. The company operates dedicated production lines for tees, tanks, and polos, and emphasizes sustainable and organic materials. The core team at headquarters numbers three employees.

Its portfolio spans tees, tanks, polos, dresses, kids and baby apparel, yoga and athleisure wear, swimwear, and dress shirts. Industries served include fashion apparel, sustainable and organic clothing, activewear, swimwear, and children’s wear.

The founders created Urth Apparel after struggling to find factories that combined quality, sustainability, and fair labor practices. The company’s stated philosophy is to “do it right, take care of the planet, take care of your workers, create clothing that lasts.” It positions itself as a one-stop partner that handles design, sourcing, and logistics, with daily communication between design teams and production floors.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product Development", "Pattern Making", "Marker Making", "Cutting & Sewing", "Screen Printing", "Textile Sublimation", "Heat Transfer", "Heat Bonding", "Sampling & Prototyping", "Technical Design", "Quality Control", "Fabric & Trim Sourcing", "Grading", "Finishing", "Packaging & Inspection", "Embroidery", "Chenille", "Digital Printing", "Sustainable Material Sourcing"], "industries": ["Apparel", "Fashion", "Sustainable clothing", "Organic clothing", "Activewear", "Swimwear", "Children''s wear", "Luxury apparel", "Knitwear", "Technical apparel"], "materials": ["Organic cotton", "Sustainable fabrics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Ethical and sustainable manufacturing with organic materials", "Production split across Italy (luxury), Peru (knitwear/basics), and USA (technical apparel)", "One-stop service from concept through production and logistics", "Dedicated production lines for basic garments (tees, tanks, polos)", "Daily communication between design teams and production floors"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Newport Beach, California -> db", "Founded in 2013 -> /about-us", "Founder started international trade cooperative for natural foods and cotton apparel from Peru -> /about-us", "Services include product development, design, pattern making, sampling, cutting/sewing, printing, finishing, packaging, inspection -> db", "Production split: luxury in Italy, knitwear/basics in Peru, technical apparel in USA -> db and /", "Dedicated production lines for tees, tanks, polos -> /", "Emphasizes sustainable and organic materials -> db and /", "Headcount of 3 employees -> db", "Serves clothing brands and designers -> /", "Product examples: tees, tanks, polos, dresses, kids/baby, yoga/athleisure, swimwear, dress shirts -> /", "Philosophy: do it right, take care of planet, workers, create lasting clothing -> /", "One-stop partner with daily communication between design and production -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom apparel manufacturer", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "3", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='urth-apparel-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Utah Breakers & Supply was established in Salt Lake City, Utah, in May 2003, beginning in a 6,000-square-foot building. The company later expanded to a 12,000-square-foot warehouse to accommodate growing inventory levels of electrical supplies.

The company buys and sells new, used, obsolete, and hard-to-find electrical equipment, with a focus on molded case circuit breakers, hardware kits, transformers, safety switches, bus plugs, MCC buckets, and starters. It reconditions and refurbishes products to meet original manufacturer specifications using state-of-the-art testing equipment, and every item is load-tested before shipment. All products carry a one-year warranty.

The business emphasizes strict reconditioning standards, same-day shipping on stocked items, and a one-year warranty as its primary differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Reconditioning and refurbishing of electrical equipment", "Load testing", "Electrical equipment testing", "Same-day shipping", "Warranty support (1-year)", "Procurement of obsolete electrical components", "Sales of circuit breakers, transformers, safety switches, bus plugs, MCC buckets, starters"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping for stocked items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping on stocked parts", "One-year warranty on all products", "Load-tested reconditioned equipment", "Strict reconditioning standards meeting manufacturer specifications", "State-of-the-art testing equipment"], "facts_used": ["Established in Salt Lake City, Utah in May 2003 -> db", "Relocated to a 12,000 square foot warehouse -> /", "Buys and sells new, used, obsolete, and hard-to-find electrical equipment -> /", "Specializes in circuit breakers, hardware kits, transformers, safety switches, bus plugs, MCC buckets, and starters -> /", "Reconditioning and refurbishing to meet manufacturer specifications -> /", "Equipped with state-of-the-art testing equipment; all products load-tested -> /", "One-year warranty on all products -> /", "Same-day shipping -> /", "Headquarters: Salt Lake City, Utah -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Utah Breakers buys and sells new, used, obsolete, and hard-to-find electrical equipment specializing in circuit breakers, hardware kits, transformers, safety switches, bus plugs, MCC buckets, and starters.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='utah-breakers-supply' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Utah Mountain Furniture operates from Salt Lake City, Utah. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed. It sells its own line of furniture directly to customers through its website.

The company handcrafts solid wood furniture in several distinct lines. The Aspen collection uses eco‑friendly dead‑standing aspen logs, while the Barnwood line is built from reclaimed wood sourced from old barns, chicken coops, sheds, and snow fencing. The Rocky Mountain line features smaller rustic logs, and the Slimline series targets space‑constrained settings. Finishes include lacquer and custom stain options.

Products are marketed to residential, cabin, and commercial buyers. The company emphasizes direct‑buy pricing and states its furniture suits "any home, cabin or commercial space."

Utah Mountain Furniture highlights its use of naturally distressed, eco‑friendly materials and the ability to tailor each piece to a customer''s specifications. The reclaimed barnwood is described as carrying "beauty, uniqueness and history," while the custom program promises "If you can dream it, we can build it."', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Handcrafted solid wood furniture manufacturing", "Custom furniture fabrication to specification", "Wood finishing (lacquer, custom stain)", "Wildlife carving", "Twig handle installation", "Custom tile work", "Reclaimed wood processing", "Dead-standing aspen log processing"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Commercial furniture", "Cabin and lodge furniture"], "materials": ["Aspen (dead standing)", "Reclaimed barnwood", "Solid wood", "Lacquer", "Custom stain"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted by expert craftsmen in Utah", "Eco\u2011friendly dead\u2011standing aspen wood", "Reclaimed barnwood with natural history", "Custom dimensions, carvings, tiles, and stains", "Direct\u2011buy pricing on exclusive lines"], "facts_used": ["Company name, HQ city/state, website -> db", "Handcrafted solid wood aspen log furniture in Utah -> /", "Eco-friendly dead standing wood for Aspen line -> /", "Reclaimed barnwood from barns, coops, sheds, snow fencing -> /", "Rocky Mountain line with smaller rustic logs -> /", "Slimline space-saving furniture -> /", "Custom furniture to desired size/spec with tiles, carvings, custom stain -> /", "Direct buy customers, exclusive line -> /", "Products suit home, cabin, commercial space -> /", "Lacquer finish on solid wood furniture -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our rustic, solid wood aspen log furniture is handcrafted by expert craftsmen here in Utah.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='utah-mountain-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Utility Wire Products, Inc. operates from a 48,000-square-foot facility on Cleveland’s industrial East Side at 3302 East 87th Street. The company was founded in 1953 by Ed Peck and Bill Milavac. Donald Anzells acquired the business in 1980, and it remains family-owned and trans-generational; current president Ronald Anzells has been with the firm for 30 years, joined by his son Ronald Anzells Jr. as plant manager and custom tooling designer in 2007.

The shop specializes in custom wire products across five major lines: point-of-purchase display racks, wire guards for lighting, fans, machinery and heaters, wire baskets, custom wire forms, and grid assemblies. Wire diameters range from .080 to .500 inch, worked in bright basic, stainless steel, and galvanized wire, with tubing, sheet metal, and plastics incorporated as needed. An on-site 3D CNC bending machine handles forming, and finishing options include powder coating, vinyl, nylon, and various plating processes. The company states it can run orders from a single unit up to 500,000 pieces.

Customers span retail merchandising (plan-o-gram display racks), industrial safety (guards for lights, fans, and high-temperature equipment), healthcare (baskets for hospital stretchers), and general manufacturing (containers for screw-machine parts). The firm works from customer designs or develops designs collaboratively.

The company’s stated motto is to deliver a ‘Quality Product in a Timely Fashion at a Fair Price that are American made,’ and its philosophy emphasizes treating every order—whether one piece or half a million—with equal importance and personal attention.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wire forming", "3D CNC wire bending", "Wire guard fabrication", "Wire display fabrication", "Wire basket fabrication", "Grid fabrication", "Powder coating", "Vinyl coating", "Nylon coating", "Plating", "Custom tooling design"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Bright basic wire", "Stainless steel wire", "Galvanized wire", "Tubing", "Sheet metal", "Plastics"], "equipment": ["3D CNC Bending Machine"], "volume": "1 to 500,000 units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Accepts orders as small as one unit", "Family-owned, trans-generational operation", "On-site 3D CNC wire bending", "In-house custom tooling design", "Multiple coating options including powder, vinyl, nylon, and plating"], "facts_used": ["Located in Cleveland, Ohio, 48,000 sq ft facility -> /about", "Founded 1953 by Ed Peck and Bill Milavac -> /about", "Donald Anzells purchased 1980, family-owned -> /about", "President Ronald Anzells 30 years, Ronald Anzells Jr. plant manager 2007 -> /about", "Motto: Quality Product in a Timely Fashion at a Fair Price that are American made -> /about", "Philosophy: treat orders 1 to 500,000 equally -> /about", "Five major product lines: POP displays, wire guards, custom wire forms, grids, baskets -> /about", "Wire diameters .080 to .500 -> /about", "Materials: bright basic, stainless steel, galvanized wire, tubing, sheet metal, plastics -> /about", "On-site 3D CNC Bending Machine -> /about", "Coatings: powder coating, vinyl, nylon, plating -> /about", "Accepts orders as small as one unit -> /about, /", "Point of Purchase Display Racks specialization -> /", "Wire Guards for Lights, Fans, Machines, Heaters -> /about", "Wire Baskets for screw machine parts, hospital stretchers -> /", "Custom tooling design in-house -> /about", "Company type: custom wire product manufacturer -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Utility Wire Products, Inc. is a custom wire product manufacturer.", "founded_year": "1953", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "1 unit", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='utility-wire-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='V-Tron Electronics Corporation operates from a 45,000-square-foot facility in Attleboro, Massachusetts. The company was incorporated in 1970 as a privately held, veteran-owned small business, initially serving the emerging Massachusetts computer industry before expanding into semiconductors, medical, military, and industrial electronics.

The company provides electronic manufacturing services including cable assemblies, wire harnesses, fiber optic assemblies, molded connector assemblies, and box build assemblies. Its process engineering team performs pre-production manufacturability analysis and reverse engineering to create documented, repeatable manufacturing roadmaps. Production is managed through a real-time, bar-coded ERP system that tracks jobs from order inception to final inspection, supporting low-to-high volume order lot sizes.

V-Tron serves defense and security, medical and life sciences, semiconductor, and industrial electronics customers. Its assemblies are built to IPC standards and tested 100 percent using Cirris 4250 scanners for cable and harness continuity, while fiber optic links are verified for insertion loss and visual defects. The company holds UL and cUL recognition for wiring harnesses (E76510) and power supply cords (E173242), plus CSA certification (LR56498-1).

President Doug Gobin emphasizes that quality and reliability are keys to survival, a philosophy reflected in an in-house training program certified to IPC-A-610, IPC/WHMA-A-620, and J-STD-001. The firm’s quality system is certified to ISO 9001:2015 and focuses on continuous improvement, on-time delivery, and scrap reduction.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL Recognized (E76510)','UL Listed (E173242)','CSA Certified (LR56498-1)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable assembly", "Wire harness assembly", "Fiber optic assembly", "Molded connector assembly (low- and high-pressure molding)", "Box build assembly", "Process engineering and pre-production manufacturability analysis", "Reverse engineering and documentation", "ERP/MRP system with bar-coded job travelers", "Custom test fixture development", "100% electrical testing (Cirris 4250)", "Fiber optic insertion loss and visual inspection", "Crimp integrity tensile testing", "In-house IPC training (IPC-A-610, IPC/WHMA-A-620, J-STD-001)", "Consigned, Kanban, and bonded inventory management"], "industries": ["Defense / Military", "Medical / Life Sciences", "Semiconductors", "Industrial Electronics"], "materials": ["Polyvinyl Chloride (PVC)", "Polyurethane (PUR)", "Polypropylene (PP)", "Thermoplastic Elastomers (TPE)", "Thermoplastic Polyamides (TPA)"], "equipment": ["Cirris 4250 scanners", "Tensile testing equipment", "Custom fabricated electrical harness test boards", "Fiber optic light meters and inspection software", "Bar-coded manufacturing software (ERP)"], "volume": "Low to high volume order lot sizes", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% functional testing on every assembly", "Real-time bar-coded ERP system for job tracking and traceability", "In-house IPC-certified training program (IPC-A-610, IPC/WHMA-A-620, J-STD-001)", "UL/cUL recognized and CSA certified", "Veteran-owned small business with process engineering support"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1970, veteran-owned small business, incorporated in Massachusetts -> /about-us", "45,000 sq ft facility in Attleboro, MA -> /about-us", "Services: cable assemblies, wire harnesses, fiber optic assemblies, molded connectors, box build -> /services", "Process engineering, reverse engineering, ERP with bar-coded job travelers -> /capabilities", "100% testing, Cirris 4250 scanners, fiber optic loss testing, crimp tensile testing -> /quality", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, UL E76510, UL E173242, CSA LR56498-1 -> /quality, /about-us", "In-house training per IPC-A-610, IPC/WHMA-A-620, J-STD-001 -> /about-us, /quality", "Industries: Defense/Military, Medical/Life Sciences, Semiconductors, Industrial Electronics -> /about-us, industries_served", "President Doug Gobin quoted on quality philosophy -> /", "Molding materials: PVC, PUR, PP, TPE, TPA -> /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Manufacturers of High-Quality Assemblies, Wire Harnesses, Box Build, and Fiber Optic Assemblies", "founded_year": "1970", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='v-tron-electronics-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='VIP (Vermont Information Processing) is headquartered in Colchester, Vermont. The company has served the beverage industry for over 50 years, though its exact founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

Its system handles AI-powered routing and logistics, route accounting, reporting and analytics, ecommerce, and product catalog management.

VIP’s customer base spans the three-tier beverage ecosystem. Suppliers use the software to gain visibility into distribution network performance and optimize brand strategy. Distributors rely on its route accounting and logistics tools to optimize daily deliveries. Retailers leverage the platform to simplify ordering and ensure shelf availability.

The company emphasizes that its technology is purpose-built for the beverage industry rather than adapted from generic solutions. It cites decades of contextual market data and an enterprise-grade AI layer tailored to beverage-specific workflows as core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["AI-powered routing and logistics", "Route accounting", "Reporting and analytics", "Ecommerce platform", "Product catalog management", "Demand planning"], "industries": ["Beverage"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AI-powered routing and logistics that reduce delivery costs and improve service levels", "Purpose-built platform for the three-tier beverage ecosystem", "Decades of contextual market data powering enterprise-grade AI", "Connects suppliers, distributors, and retailers in a single platform", "Industry-leading route accounting and logistics for modern delivery complexities"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Colchester, Vermont -> db", "550K total users, 50-state footprint, 50+ years industry experience -> /", "Acquired Encompass Technologies -> /", "Serves beverage suppliers, distributors, retailers -> /", "Platform includes reporting & analytics, routing & logistics, ecommerce -> /", "AI-powered routing and logistics capabilities -> /", "Purpose-built for beverage industry, decades of data -> /"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "VIP connects beverage industry suppliers, distributors, and retailers with purpose-built technology that simplifies complexity, strengthens relationships, and empowers smarter decisions across the entire ecosystem.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vip-vermont-information-processing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='VIP Rubber and Plastic operates from Minden, Nevada, where it has been manufacturing rubber and plastic products since 1961. The company was founded by Howard Vipperman Sr., known as “Big Vip,” who entered the rubber industry as a gasket cutter after serving in the armed forces. It remains a family-owned American manufacturer now led by subsequent generations.

The company specializes in custom rubber extrusions, plastic extrusions, rubber sheet and roll products, molded rubber parts, and plastic pipe and tubing. It also offers custom rubber compounding and a suite of value-added fabrication services under its Vip+ Services program, positioning itself as a one-stop shop. Production includes solid rod, cord, profiles, seals, gaskets, window and door seals, and vinyl spline.

VIP serves a range of industries including aerospace, agriculture, automotive, architectural glass and metal, and construction. Its facility is an approved manufacturer for several Boeing material specifications and holds AS9100 certification, supplying top aerospace organizations. The company also produces parts for custom applications across virtually every industry.

The company emphasizes its family-owned heritage, generations of manufacturing experience, and the integration of Excalibur Extrusions’ plastic extrusion capabilities. It highlights its AS9100-certified quality system, ITAR registration, and the fact that all products are manufactured in the USA as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','ISO9001','ITAR','ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rubber extrusion", "Plastic extrusion", "Rubber sheet manufacturing", "Molded rubber parts", "Custom rubber compounding", "Value-added fabrication (Vip+ Services)", "Plastic pipe extrusion", "Extruded window and door seals", "Vinyl spline production", "Custom plastic fabrication", "Rubber profiles, solid rod & cord", "Plastic tubing"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Agriculture", "Automotive", "Architectural Glass & Metal", "Construction", "Custom"], "materials": ["Rubber", "Plastic", "Custom rubber compounds"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1961", "Approved manufacturer for Boeing material specifications", "AS9100-certified quality management system", "Vip+ Services value-added fabrication and one-stop-shop capability", "All products manufactured in the USA"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Minden, Nevada -> db", "Founded 1961 by Howard Vipperman Sr. -> /", "Family-owned American manufacturer -> /", "Founder served in armed forces -> /", "Specializes in custom rubber extrusions, plastic extrusions, rubber sheet, molded rubber, plastic pipe/tubing -> db, /", "Offers custom rubber compounding -> /", "Vip+ Services value-added fabrication -> /", "Approved manufacturer for Boeing material specifications -> /", "AS9100 certified -> db, /", "ITAR registered -> db", "ISO9001 certified -> db", "ROHS compliant -> db", "Industries served: Aerospace, Agriculture, Automotive, Architectural Glass & Metal, Construction, Custom -> /", "Excalibur Extrusions merged -> /", "All products manufactured in USA -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in custom rubber extrusions, plastic extrusions, rubber sheet products, molded rubber products, plastic pipe and tubing.", "founded_year": "1961", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vip-plastics-and-rubber-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='VMS operates from a 12,000-square-foot facility in West Rutland, Vermont, conveniently located near major transportation routes to New York, New Hampshire, Massachusetts, Maine, and Canada. The business has more than three decades of industry experience and was acquired by Jessica Dambrackas in 2011 when she purchased the former Rutland Industries, continuing a legacy of contract manufacturing, fulfillment, and packaging services.

The company provides a range of outsourced services including quality control, distribution, inventory management, kitting, packaging, assembly, pick-and-pack, e-commerce fulfillment, warehousing, and cross-docking. Its climate-controlled warehouse and loading docks accommodate various truck sizes, while specialized software integrates with e-commerce shopping carts for rapid order processing. The team handles everything from basic hand assembly to comprehensive offsite manufacturing and packaging divisions, operating under lean manufacturing principles.

VMS serves clients across diverse sectors such as electronics manufacturing, food packaging, e-commerce, fashion, and publishing. Notable customers have included the Rutland Herald for bundle distribution and startup companies requiring flexible warehousing and accurate order fulfillment. The company''s clientele spans both large and small businesses seeking to reduce overhead and streamline supply chains.

