UPDATE companies SET description='Valley Woodworks LLC was founded in 2022 by Jonathan Dias in Palmer, Massachusetts. Dias, a graduate of Springfield College with a degree in Business Administration and a minor in Entrepreneurial Studies, started the company after deciding he could not spend his career in an office. He began building furniture by hand with the goal of creating pieces that lacked the commercial, mass-produced feel of typical retail offerings.

The workshop produces custom tables and furniture on a commission basis. Each piece starts as a solid hardwood slab, hand-selected for grain, moisture content, and character. The company uses no veneers, plywood cores, or engineered composites. Finishes are hand-rubbed hardwax oils that protect the wood while leaving the grain visible and pores open.

Valley Woodworks serves residential clients seeking heirloom-quality furniture for their homes. Customers engage directly with the maker through a design consultation, resulting in one-of-a-kind dining tables, desks, and other pieces intended to anchor a living space for generations. The company does not sell through retailers or maintain inventory; every item is made to order.

Dias founded the business to counter what he describes as a click-to-buy culture that prioritizes speed over longevity. The stated mission is to keep the art of fine furniture making alive by delivering pieces that are passed down rather than replaced. The company’s differentiator is its commitment to solid-wood construction and transparent finishing that shows the material’s natural character.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Solid hardwood milling", "Hand-rubbed hardwax oil finishing", "Commission-based production", "Wood selection and grading"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Solid hardwood", "Hardwax oil"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Solid hardwood construction with no veneers or plywood cores", "Hand-rubbed hardwax oil finishes that preserve wood''s natural grain and pores", "Custom commission model with direct designer-maker collaboration", "Founded to counter mass-produced, disposable furniture culture"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2022 by Jonathan Dias -> /about", "Located in Palmer, Massachusetts -> db", "Produces custom tables and furniture from solid hardwood slabs -> /", "Uses hand-rubbed hardwax oil finishes -> /", "No veneers or plywood cores -> /", "Founder Jonathan Dias holds degree from Springfield College -> /about", "Company aims to counter mass-produced furniture culture -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Every Valley Woodworks piece begins as a solid hardwood slab, hand-selected for grain, moisture content, and character.", "founded_year": "2022", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='valley-woodworks-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Vault Furniture operates from Caldwell, Idaho, where it handcrafts furniture and home décor. The company was co-founded by Brandi, who serves as designer, though the founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The shop produces reclaimed-wood shelving units, wall-mounted desks, tables, benches, carts, vases, wine racks, pet feeders and mounting brackets. Every piece is made to order using reclaimed old-growth pine, sustainably sourced ash and black walnut, American steel and GREENGUARD-certified low-VOC finishes. Production takes place in the company’s Caldwell facility, where woodworking, metal fabrication and finishing are done by hand.

Vault Furniture sells directly to homeowners and works with interior designers and commercial clients seeking custom pieces. The catalog includes residential furniture and home accessories, with examples such as the Asymmetrical Side Table, Modern Industrial Coffee Table and vertical wall vases. The company also supplies shelf brackets and mounting hardware for DIY installations.

