UPDATE companies SET description='Velmar Food Services operates from Phoenix, Arizona, where it was founded in 1974 by Richard and Judith Barton. The company began with recipes developed by Richard''s father, a culinary craftsman who created the perfect burrito, and initially served mobile food services before expanding to supply unified school districts across Arizona and California. Now a third-generation family-run business, Velmar remains headquartered at 4420 N. 42nd Avenue in Phoenix.

The company manufactures its own Arizona Gold brand of Mexican cuisine — including burritos, beans, cheese, green chiles, fresh eggs and choice meats — using locally produced tortillas and select spices. In addition to manufacturing, Velmar provides foodservice distribution of top-label brands to restaurants, delis, convenience stores, healthcare facilities and correctional operations. Its facilities include a large warehouse and freezer space that it also leases to other food businesses for pallet storage, helping them manage seasonal demand spikes.

Velmar''s customer base spans restaurants, delis, convenience stores, healthcare facilities, correctional operations and school districts.

