UPDATE companies SET description='Vermillion Inc. was established in 1965 in Wichita, Kansas, as a manufacturer of custom cable assemblies.

The company operates a 43,000-square-foot manufacturing facility where it produces bulk cable, custom-designed cable assemblies, and molded assemblies. Its capabilities span engineering and design consultation, prototyping, and initial production runs, supported by in-house testing equipment such as DIT-MCO 2500 and 2650 MTA models. Vermillion works with a wide range of conductor, shielding, and jacketing materials, including its proprietary Vermalloy® alloys, Aracon® aramid fibers, and high-temperature fluoropolymers.

Vermillion serves the military and aerospace sectors, with customers such as Rockwell Collins, which named the company its Wire and Cable Supplier of the Year in 2009. The firm’s products are used in secure voice communications, avionics, and other defense applications requiring high-reliability interconnects.

Vermillion differentiates itself through its long-standing quality certifications—ISO 9001 since 1996 and AS9100C since 2003—and its receipt of the Kansas Award for Excellence three years running.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2008','AS9100C','J-STD-001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable design and engineering", "Bulk cable manufacturing", "Cable assembly and molding", "Prototyping and low-volume production", "J-STD-001 certified soldering", "Electrical testing (DIT-MCO 2500/2650)", "Shielding application (Vermalloy\u00ae, Aracon\u00ae, metal foils, Mylar)", "Jacketing (ETFE, PTFE, PFA, LSZH, braided, blown-on)", "Conductor tinning and plating (tin, nickel, silver)", "Wire and cable processing"], "industries": ["Military", "Aerospace", "Defense"], "materials": ["Tinned Copper", "Nickel Plated Copper", "Silver Plated Copper", "Vermalloy 622", "Vermalloy 3948", "Flattened Tinned Copper", "Aracon\u00ae Aramid Fibers", "Copper Foil", "Aluminum Foil", "Copper Mylar", "Aluminum Mylar", "150\u00b0 ETFE", "200\u00b0 ETFE", "Polyethylene (Low Smoke Zero Halogen)", "PTFE", "PFA", "Polyester", "Nomex", "Kevlar", "PEEK", "Teflon Impregnated Fiberglass", "Fiberglass", "Neoprene", "EPDM", "Viton\u00ae"], "equipment": ["DIT-MCO 2500", "DIT-MCO 2650 MTA"], "volume": "Prototype to initial production orders", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1965 -> /", "Headquarters in Wichita, Kansas -> /", "43,000 sq ft manufacturing facility -> /", "ISO 9001 certified since 1996 -> /", "Kansas Award for Excellence 1996, 1997, 1998 -> /", "Custom cable design and engineering capability -> /", "Bulk cable production -> /", "Molded assemblies -> /", "Military and aerospace industries served -> /", "Vermalloy\u00ae shielding material -> /", "AS9100C certified since 2003 -> /quality", "J-STD-001 Wire & Cable Supplier certification -> /quality", "Rockwell Collins Wire and Cable Supplier of the Year 2009 -> /quality", "DIT-MCO 2500 and 265