UPDATE companies SET description='Vermont Electric Power Company (VELCO), headquartered in Rutland, Vermont, was created in 1956 as the nation''s first statewide, transmission-only electric utility. The company was formed to build and operate an interconnected high-voltage transmission grid that would deliver and share access to clean power, including hydroelectric resources, across Vermont. Ownership is held by the state''s 17 distribution utilities and a public benefits corporation, and its for-profit structure is designed to return value to those owners, their customers, and all Vermonters.

VELCO owns and operates the high-voltage transmission system that moves electricity from generation sources to local distribution companies, which then serve homes and businesses. The company does not directly serve retail customers. Its work encompasses transmission system planning, grid reliability management, and the interconnection of generation resources. VELCO also publishes an annual ESG report and maintains a safety culture focused on employee well-being.

The primary customers are Vermont''s 17 distribution utilities, including municipal departments such as Burlington Electric Department, Stowe Electric Department, and others listed as owners. Through these utilities, VELCO''s transmission network ultimately serves residential, commercial, and industrial end-users across the state. The company also engages with regional energy stakeholders to provide a unified voice on transmission and clean energy issues.

VELCO distinguishes itself as the first transmission-only company of its kind in the United States, a model that remains unique. Its ownership structure and mandate to return value to utility owners and ratepayers set it apart from investor-owned utilities. The company emphasizes environmental stewardship, sustainability initiatives, and a commitment to a reliable, affordable, and secure grid as core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["High-voltage transmission grid operation", "Transmission system planning and construction", "Interconnection of renewable generation resources", "Grid reliability and security management", "Regional energy policy advocacy"], "industries": ["Electric power transmission", "Clean energy", "Electric utilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Nation''s first statewide, transmission-only company", "Ownership by 17 distribution utilities and a public benefits corporation", "For-profit structure returning value to owners, customers, and Vermonters", "Environmental stewardship embedded in company culture", "Safety as a core value with goal of zero incidents"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1956 -> /about", "Headquarters Rutland, Vermont -> db", "Ownership: 17 distribution utilities and a public benefits corporation -> /about", "First statewide transmission-only company in the nation -> /about", "Mission: serve as a trusted partner -> /about", "Vision: create a sustainable Vermont -> /about", "Operates high-voltage transmission grid -> /about", "Does not directly serve individual homes/businesses -> /", "Delivers power to local distribution companies -> /", "2024 ESG Report published -> /about", "Safety culture core value -> /about", "Environmental stewardship embodied in culture -> /about", "List of distribution utility owners (Barton Village, Burlington Electric, etc.) -> db"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "VELCO is the nation''s first statewide, transmission-only company, created in 1956 to build and operate an interconnected electric transmission grid in order to deliver and share access in Vermont to clean power, including hydro.", "founded_year": "1956", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vermont-electric-power-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
