UPDATE companies SET description='Versa Electronics, Inc. is based in New Hope, Minnesota. The company traces its roots to 1979 when Versa Co. was formed as a parent to several manufacturing ventures, including Versa Electronics. In 1994, Kevin Johnsrud, who had joined as CFO in 1990, acquired the assets of Versa Electronics and established Versa Electronics Co. The business separated from the Versa Companies in 2007 to become Electronic Technologies, LLC, doing business as Versa Electronics. Johnsrud remains CEO.

Versa provides electronic manufacturing services (EMS) with a focus on printed circuit board assembly (PCBA), box build, cable and wire harness assembly, testing, calibration, conformal coating, and potting. The facility supports both automated surface-mount and through-hole production, including BGA placement, automated optical inspection, and X-ray solder inspection. The company maintains over 6,000 inventoried components for build-to-order and consignment programs, and offers quick changeover and in-process engineering change management for short- to medium-run volumes.

Versa serves medical device, consumer electronics, industrial, communications, and finance sectors. A noted customer is MarCum Technologies, an ice-fishing electronics brand whose underwater cameras and sonar units are assembled at Versa''s plant. The company is FDA registered and holds ISO 13485:2016 for medical manufacturing, and is an Apple MFi licensee for accessory production.

Versa emphasizes flexibility, reliability, and consultative communication. The firm highlights its ability to manage variable demand and lead times, provide turnkey or consigned inventory models, and deliver on-time delivery metrics. Its quality system is certified to ISO 9001:2015 and compliant with IPC-A-610 Class 1-3 and IPC/WHMA-620 standards.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','ISO 9001:2015','FDA Registered','IPC-A-610J Class 1-3','IPC Corporate Member','SMTA Corporate Member','Apple MFi Developer Licensed','CSA','TUV','ETL','UL','FCC','ROHS','REACH','Conflict Minerals Compliant','EPA','FAR','NAFTA','MDH','MPCA','HCHW','CAN TSSA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed Circuit Board Assembly (PCBA)", "Surface Mount Technology (SMT) Assembly", "Through-Hole Assembly", "Box Build Assembly / System Integration", "Cable & Wire Harness Assembly", "Testing & Calibration", "Conformal Coating & Potting", "Global Supply Chain & Material Management", "Product Lifecycle Support", "Quick Changeover", "In-Process ECO Management", "Circuit Board & Sub-Assembly", "Device Assembly", "Complete BGA Capability", "Wire Termination", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "X-ray Soldering Inspection", "Prototyping", "Short- to Medium-Run Production", "Turnkey Manufacturing", "Consignment Inventory Programs", "Kanban Inventory Management", "Design for Manufacturability Feedback", "Component Procurement", "Legacy Product Support"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Consumer Electronics", "Industrial", "Communications", "Finance"], "materials": ["FR-4", "flex circuit", "rigid-flex hybrid circuits"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 6,000 inventoried components for build-to-order and consignment programs", "Automated surface-mount and through-hole lines with BGA, AOI, and X-ray inspection", "Quick changeover and in-process engineering change management", "ISO 13485:2016 and ISO 9001:2015 certified, FDA registered", "Apple MFi licensed for accessory manufacturing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 as Versa Co. -> /about", "Kevin Johnsrud acquired Versa Electronics assets in 1994 -> /about", "Headquarters in New Hope, Minnesota -> db", "ISO 13485:2016 and ISO 9001:2015 certified, FDA registered -> /about", "Over 6,000 inventoried components for build-to-order -> /about", "Services: PCBA, box build, cable assembly, testing, conformal coating -> /services", "Industries served: Medical, Consumer, Industrial, Communications, Finance -> /", "MarCum Technologies case study (ice fishing electronics) -> /", "Apple MFi Developer Licensed -> /about", "Automated surface mount and through-hole production, BGA capability, AOI, X-ray inspection -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Versa Electronics has provided electronic manufacturing services (EMS), contract manufacturing, and OEM experience towards the achievement of each client''s product lifecycle and business success goals.", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='versa-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Versa-Tech Metal Fab Inc has operated from Portland, Oregon since 1978.

The shop centers on heavy structural and plate fabrication. Its equipment lineup includes an Omax 55100 waterjet, a 5,000-watt Trumpf CO2 laser with auto-load tables, a Whitney 3700 ATC punch/plasma combination, and a Kinetic K4000 plate processor with dual Hypertherm HPR400XD high-definition plasma heads capable of cutting steel up to three inches thick. Forming capacity reaches 50 feet in a single hit via a tandem Cincinnati 1,500-ton and Pacific 1,000-ton press brake pair, supported by five additional brakes ranging from 60 to 500 tons. Four hydraulic shears handle up to 30-foot lengths, while two Roundo plate rolls, multiple bandsaws, a cold saw, and a Piranha 140-ton ironworker round out the floor. Welding covers MIG, TIG, and stud welding backed by numerous AWS certifications.

