UPDATE companies SET description='VoltServer is headquartered in East Greenwich, Rhode Island. Founded by Stephen Eaves, who serves as CEO, the company has spent over a decade deploying its Digital Electricity™ fault-managed power systems across critical infrastructure.

Its platform includes real-time telemetry, remote firmware updates, and policy-based control, supported by a team of solution engineers who assist with system design at no charge. VoltServer reports more than 1,000 building installations and 40,000 circuits in large venues.

VoltServer serves service providers building 5G and Wi-Fi networks, transportation hubs such as airports and ports, enterprise campuses, industrial manufacturing facilities automating production, data centers adding AI server racks, and building electrification projects for smart real estate. The company also lists telecom, data center, enterprise, and transportation as core markets.

VoltServer differentiates itself through inherent safety — its Class 4 fault-managed power stops hazardous current within milliseconds — rapid deployment that often avoids conduit and permitting, and NEC recognition in the 2023 code. The technology reduces material use, qualifies for LEED credits, and earned Cisco Select Developer status for integration with industrial IoT switches.', certifications=ARRAY['NEC 2023 (Fault-Managed Power Systems / Class 4 Power)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Digital Electricity\u2122 fault-managed power systems", "Packet energy transfer technology", "Hybrid fiber cable power delivery", "Real-time device telemetry and monitoring", "Remote software updates without power interruption", "Policy-based control and scheduling", "Free solution engineering and system design support", "Class 4 power system installation (NEC 2023)", "Integration with Cisco IE Series PoE switches", "Digital Edge Solutions for IIoT"], "industries": ["Service Provider", "Transportation Networks", "Enterprise Buildings and Campuses", "Industrial Manufacturing", "Data Centers", "Building Electrification", "Telecom", "Enterprise", "Transportation"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Transmitter unit", "Receiver unit", "Hybrid fiber cable", "Digital Edge Solutions"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fault-managed power that stops hazardous current within milliseconds", "Delivers power over existing data pathways or hybrid fiber cable", "NEC-recognized Class 4 power system (2023)", "Free solution engineering support for design integration", "Cisco Select Developer partner for IIoT power solutions"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: East Greenwich, Rhode Island -> db", "Founder: Stephen Eaves -> db, /about", "10-year deployment history -> db, /about", "Digital Electricity\u2122 fault-managed power systems -> db, /about", "1,000+ building installations -> /about", "40,000+ circuits & large venues -> /about", "99.9% customer satisfaction -