UPDATE companies SET description='W. L. Gore & Associates, Inc. operates its Paper Mill West facility in Newark, Delaware. The company was founded in 1958 by Bill and Vieve Gore, who started the enterprise in their family home. Today, the business remains a global materials science organization with approximately 13,000 associates spanning five continents.

Its portfolio includes high-performance cables and assemblies, filtration media, gaskets and sealants, medical devices, proton exchange membranes for hydrogen production, thermal insulation, and venting solutions.

The company serves a broad set of industries: aerospace and defense, automotive and electrified vehicles, telecommunications, electronics, semiconductor, energy, life sciences, industrial manufacturing, fire and public safety, apparel and textiles, chemicals, and test and measurement. Concrete examples include microwave RF test cables for aerospace and semiconductor applications, GORE-TEX consumer and professional fabrics, implantable medical devices under the Gore Medical brand, and outdoor gear from SITKA Gear.

