UPDATE companies SET description='WORLD electronics operates from Reading, Pennsylvania, where the company has been based since 1999. The business traces its roots to 1991, and in 1986 Joe Rado purchased the company, moving it from West Chester to Morgantown before designing the current Reading facility. Under Rado''s leadership the firm grew from eight people to over 100 employees. Since 2018 the Rado family''s women have led the company, which holds WBENC certification as a woman-owned business.

The company provides turnkey printed circuit board assembly and box-build services for low-to-medium-volume, high-mix production. Its shop runs six independent surface-mount lines, through-hole soldering, a Kulicke & Soffa 8090 wedge wire bonder, automated optical inspection, X-ray inspection, in-circuit and functional test, burn-in and temperature cycling, component programming, rework, cleaning and pin insertion. Engineering support covers design for manufacturability, test development, PCB layout and supply-chain management.

Customers span communications, networking, medical, defense and industrial-control sectors, ranging from major OEMs to high-tech start-ups. The firm handles both tin-lead and RoHS-compliant assemblies, offering surface finishes such as HASL, nickel-gold, OSP and immersion silver.

Joe Rado''s motto — “We do things other people don''t want to do” — still drives the culture. A flexible floor layout enables quick setup and teardown for prototype runs, while an integrated bar-coded ERP system provides real-time job tracking. The company emphasizes a supportive workplace and a “have some fun” attitude.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS','WBENC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB assembly (surface mount and through-hole)", "Box build / higher-level assembly", "Turnkey PCB services", "New Product Introduction (NPI)", "Engineering design and development (DFM, DFT)", "PCB design and layout", "Component procurement and warehousing", "Component rework", "Component programming", "PCB cleaning", "Pin insertion", "Burn-in and temperature cycling", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "X-ray inspection", "In-circuit testing (ICT)", "Functional testing", "Test set development", "Wire bonding (wedge-wedge, gold and aluminum)", "Supply chain management", "RoHS-compliant manufacturing", "Rapid prototype production", "Custom test fixture development", "Environmental testing"], "industries": ["communications", "networking", "medical", "defense", "industrial control"], "materials": ["tin-lead solder", "RoHS-compliant (lead-free) solder", "HASL surface finish", "nickel-gold (Ni/Au) surface finish", "OSP surface finish", "immersion silver (I-Ag) surface finish", "gold wire (ASTM F72-90)", "aluminum wire (F487-88)"], "equipment": ["6 independent surface mount lines", "Kulicke & Soffa 8090 large area wedge wire-bonding machine", "Automated optical inspection (AOI) system", "X-ray inspection system", "In-circuit test (ICT) fixtures", "Burn-in and temperature cycling chambers", "Bar-coded ERP tracking system"], "volume": "Low to medium volume, high mix; prototypes to production", "lead_time": "Production runs: 4-6 weeks; turnkey assemblies: 2-3 weeks; quick-turn prototypes: 5-10 business days with customer-supplied components", "tolerances": "12-mil pitch for leaded 