UPDATE companies SET description='West Hartford Solar is based in West Hartford, Connecticut. The company was founded by Dan Hovey with a mission to make solar energy accessible, personal, and ethical. What began as a solo endeavor has grown into a regional team serving customers across New England.

The firm operates as a licensed solar installer covering Connecticut, Massachusetts, and New York. It manages projects in-house from design and permitting through installation and system activation. Installation crews work directly in Connecticut, while partnerships with Earthlight Technologies and New York State Solar Farm extend coverage into Massachusetts and New York. A team of senior consultants supports clients across western Massachusetts, the Connecticut River Valley, southeastern Connecticut, and the Northwest Hills.

Customers include homeowners, businesses, schools, nonprofits, and municipalities. The company has worked with corporate facilities, housing authorities, and local government projects to build custom solar solutions that lower operating costs and meet sustainability goals.

West Hartford Solar emphasizes transparent pricing with access to multiple financing options and no hidden markups. Each client receives a dedicated local representative backed by a regional support team, guiding them from initial consultation through post-installation questions. The founder’s original goal — making solar stress-free and ethical — continues to shape the company’s approach.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar system design", "Permitting", "Installation", "System activation", "Project coordination", "Financing options consultation", "Energy savings estimation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Education", "Nonprofit", "Municipal"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house design, permitting, installation, and activation", "Regional partnerships with Earthlight Technologies (MA) and New York State Solar Farm (NY)", "Transparent pricing with multiple financing options and no hidden markups", "Dedicated local representative backed by a knowledgeable regional team", "Licensed installer serving Connecticut, Massachusetts, and New York"], "facts_used": ["Founded by Dan Hovey -> /", "Mission: make solar accessible, personal, ethical -> /", "Started as solo journey, grown into regional team serving New England -> /", "Licensed solar installer serving CT, MA, NY -> /", "In-house design, permitting, installation, activation -> /", "Install crews in CT, partners with Earthlight Technologies (MA) and New York State Solar Farm (NY) -> /", "Team includes Dan Hovey (Owner), Annie (Co-Founder), Eric Campbell, Kyle Thomas, Jon Gorman, Nelson Plaza -> /", "Serves homeowners, businesses, schools, nonprofits, municipalities -> /", "Transparent pricing, multiple financing options, no hidden markups -> /", "Personal local rep backed by regional team -> /", "30% federal tax credit mentioned -> /", "Headquarters: West Hartford, Connecticut -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "West Hartford Solar is a licensed solar installer serving Connecticut, Massachusetts, and New York.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='west-hartford-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The West Tennessee Solar Exhibit is located in Stanton, Tennessee. The project originated from a $62.5-million allocation of federal American Recovery and Reinvestment Act funds to the Tennessee Department of Economic and Community Development in 2009. The department contracted with the University of Tennessee to oversee the creation and operation of the solar farm through the UT Research Foundation. Signal Energy, LLC of Chattanooga designed and built the array in 2011, with grid connection achieved in early 2012.

The facility spans more than 25 acres and houses approximately 21,000 fixed-tilt, ground-mounted photovoltaic panels. Electricity generated is sold under purchase agreements with Chickasaw Electric Cooperative and the Tennessee Valley Authority. In addition to power production, the site hosts SPECTRUM, an educational exhibit that walks visitors through the history, current technology, and future of solar energy in Tennessee through interactive displays and games.

The operation serves the advanced energy and renewable energy sectors, with direct utility customers including Chickasaw Electric Cooperative and TVA. Partners in the effort include Oak Ridge National Laboratory, the Tennessee Advanced Energy Business Council, the Tennessee Renewable Energy & Economic Development Council, and multiple state agencies.

The initiative was launched under the Volunteer State Solar Initiative, a comprehensive program focused on job creation, education, renewable power production, and technology commercialization. The exhibit aims to connect visitors with practical solar applications and inspire the next generation of energy professionals.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar power generation", "Photovoltaic array operation", "Educational exhibit management", "Electricity distribution via power purchase agreements"], "industries": ["Advanced energy", "Solar power", "Renewable energy", "Education"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Fixed-tilt ground-mounted photovoltaic array (21,000 panels)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Name: West Tennessee Solar Exhibit -> db", "Location: Stanton, Tennessee -> db", "Description: 25 acres, 21,000 panels, purchase agreements with Chickasaw Electric Cooperative and TVA -> db", "Funding: $62.5M ARRA funds in 2009 to TN Dept of ECD -> /", "Contract: TN Dept of ECD contracted with UT to oversee creation and operation -> /", "Builder: Signal Energy, LLC designed and built array in 2011 -> /", "Grid connection: early 2012 -> /", "Operator: UT Research Foundation -> /", "Exhibit: SPECTRUM educational exhibit with interactive displays -> /", "Partners: Oak Ridge National Laboratory, TVA, state agencies, etc. -> /", "Industries: advanced energy, solar power -> db, /", "Website: http://solarfarm.tennessee.edu/ -> db"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Electricity generated is distributed through purchase agreements with local utility Chickasaw Electric Cooperative and Tennessee Valley Authority.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='west-tennessee-solar-exhibit' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='West Virginia Steel Corporation is based in Poca, West Virginia, and operates as one of seven companies under the RMIS Corporation umbrella, a group that traces its origins to 1978. The business began with a focus on mine supplies and grew through acquisitions to offer a broad range of industrial products and services.

The company functions as a comprehensive steel supplier and fabricator, maintaining one of the largest steel inventories in West Virginia. Its fabrication shop works to AISC guidelines and includes a CNC‑controlled plasma burning table that cuts plate up to 6 inches thick. The operation handles structural steel packages up to 2,000 tons, producing components for material‑handling systems, cleaning systems, preparation facilities, heavy construction equipment, and specialty buildings. Turn‑key building solutions cover medical, educational, religious, manufacturing, and commercial projects.

Primary customers are in the mining, industrial, and commercial sectors across Appalachia, the Midwest, and internationally. Concrete projects include total steel packages for coal preparation plants, the Laidley Towers office building in Charleston, and structural modules for U.S. naval battleships. The firm also serves medical, educational, and religious construction markets.

West Virginia Steel Corporation emphasizes its extensive in‑stock inventory and ability to deliver complete, fabricated steel packages on an expedited basis. The parent RMIS group’s philosophy is to supply everything a customer needs, leveraging a network of manufacturers and suppliers to meet requirements cost‑effectively.', certifications=ARRAY['AISC','MSHA','State Fire Marshal']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "CNC plasma plate cutting", "Turn-key steel building solutions", "Material handling system fabrication", "Preparation plant fabrication", "Heavy construction equipment fabrication", "Specialty building fabrication"], "industries": ["Mining", "Industrial", "Commercial", "Medical", "Educational", "Religious", "Manufacturing", "Naval"], "materials": ["Steel", "Plate steel (up to 6\")", "Conveyor belt", "Used conveyor belt"], "equipment": ["CNC controlled plasma burning table", "15-ton boom trucks", "17-ton boom trucks", "23.5-ton boom trucks", "40-ton cranes", "60-ton cranes", "65-ton cranes"], "volume": "Up to 2,000 tons fabrication capacity", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One of the largest steel inventories in West Virginia", "Fabrication to AISC guidelines with CNC plasma cutting up to 6\u2033 plate", "Structural steel fabrication capacity up to 2,000 tons", "Turn\u2011key building solutions for commercial, industrial, and institutional projects", "Integrated network of seven RMIS companies for broad product and service access"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Poca, WV -> db", "Part of RMIS Corporation group founded in 1978 -> /about-us", "Steel supplier and fabricator -> /", "One of the largest steel inventories in West Virginia -> /", "Fabrication per AISC guidelines -> /", "Turn-key steel solutions for various building types -> /", "Fabricated prep plants, Laidley Towers, naval modules -> /", "CNC plasma burning table cuts up to 6\" plate -> /, /services", "Steel fabrication capacity up to 2,000 tons -> /services", "Serves mining, industrial, commercial, medical, educational, religious, manufacturing sectors -> /, /about-us", "Equipment: CNC plasma table, boom trucks (15, 17, 23.5 ton), cranes (40, 60, 65 ton) -> /, /services", "Certifications: AISC, MSHA, State Fire Marshal -> /, /services", "Materials: Steel, plate steel, conveyor belt -> /, /about-us", "Volume: up to 2,000 tons fabrication capacity -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "West Virginia Steel Corporation is a comprehensive steel supplier and fabricator for the industrial, commercial, and mining industry.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='west-virginia-steel-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Westec Plastics Corporation was founded in 1969 in Livermore, California, by Paul Biery and his wife Karen. Paul, a toolmaker who had recently returned from the Vietnam War, purchased his first injection molding machine from a farmer''s barn in Gilroy and began sampling his own tools in-house.

The company specializes in precision plastic injection molding, offering in-house tooling, two-shot molding, insert and overmolding, clean room manufacturing (ISO Class 7 and 8), secondary operations and assembly, and advanced metrology with CMM inspection. Its production floor houses 23 injection molding machines ranging from 28 to 610 tons, including three dedicated two-shot machines, all integrated with a real-time monitoring system. Advanced tooling capabilities include a Makino F3 vertical machining center, an Agie Charmilles FORM 20 EDM, and Mantle 3D-printed steel tooling for accelerated lead times.

Westec serves regulated and high-precision industries including medical devices, biotech and pharmaceutical, electronics, aerospace and defense, and select consumer and food-and-beverage applications. Customer references include medical device companies such as those represented by Sandy G. and Sara N., and a biotech diagnostics firm cited by Victor B. The firm''s ISO 13485:2016 certification supports regulated programs requiring contamination control, DNA-free molding, and full validation documentation.

Rooted in toolmaking, Westec differentiates itself by combining in-house tool design and fabrication with a flexible sourcing strategy that leverages domestic and offshore partners. The company emphasizes process control through statistical process control, first article inspection, and real-time production monitoring, aiming to reduce supply chain risk while maintaining tight tolerances and consistent quality from prototype through full-scale production.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "In-house tool design and fabrication", "Two-shot molding", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Clean room manufacturing (ISO Class 7 & 8)", "Secondary operations and assembly", "Advanced metrology & CMM inspection", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Mold flow analysis", "Mold design and prototyping", "3D printed steel tooling (Mantle)", "Bridge tooling", "Statistical process control (SPC)", "First article inspection (FAI)", "Process validation support", "Gage R&R studies", "Certificate of Compliance (CoC)", "Raw material certifications", "RoHS/REACH compliance documentation", "Real-time production monitoring", "Automation and cobot integration", "Vibration welding", "Ultrasonic welding", "Laser engraving", "Pad printing"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Biotech & pharmaceutical", "Electronics", "Aerospace & defense", "Consumer", "Food and beverage"], "materials": ["Engineering-grade resins", "High-performance polymers"], "equipment": ["Arburg 88T molding machine", "Milacron 610T molding machine", "Milacron 110T molding machine", "Sumitomo 385T electric injection molding machine", "Van Dorn 85T hydraulic molding machine", "Van Dorn 170T hydraulic molding machine", "Sumitomo 198T electric molding machines (2)", "Makino F3 Vertical Machining Center", "Agie Charmilles FORM 20 EDM", "Keyence IM-7030T Instant Measurement System", "Micro-Vu Excel 652UC CMM", "Branson Mini II Linear Vibration We