UPDATE companies SET description='Westinghouse Electric Co LLC, headquartered in Hopkins, South Carolina, traces its origins to 1869 when George Westinghouse founded Westinghouse Electric Company. The enterprise began with innovations in rail travel and electric power, later extending into nuclear energy in 1957 with the world''s first commercial pressurized water reactor.

Today the company designs and manufactures nuclear reactors, fuel, and components, supplying over 100,000 nuclear parts annually. Its technology powers 57 percent of the world''s nuclear power plants, maintains nearly two-thirds of the global fleet, and fuels 40 percent of that fleet. With approximately 12,500 employees across more than 100 locations in 23 countries, Westinghouse provides integrated services for routine maintenance, emergent issues, and new plant deployment, including the AP1000 Generation III+ reactor with passive safety features.

The company serves utilities and nuclear operators worldwide. Recent customers include Polish suppliers for the first AP1000 unit at Lubiatowo-Kopalino, the Ringhals plant in Sweden for clevis bolt replacement, and the ITER project in Europe for vacuum vessel sectors. Its services span operating plant support, new plant construction, and innovation programs such as the PWROG AI Assistant.

Westinghouse positions itself as an indispensable partner for global nuclear expansion, stating that the world cannot meet energy demands without nuclear and cannot build more nuclear without Westinghouse. Its differentiation rests on a legacy of first-of-a-kind technology, industrial scale, and a vision to shape the next generation of nuclear innovation.', certifications=ARRAY['ASME']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Nuclear reactor design and supply (AP1000, PWR)", "Nuclear fuel manufacturing and supply", "Nuclear component manufacturing (100,000+ parts annually)", "Plant maintenance and outage services", "Integrated LMS service", "User support service", "Nuclear engineering and licensing support", "New plant deployment and construction support", "Innovation and advanced technology development (e.g., PWROG AI Assistant)", "Passive safety system design"], "industries": ["Nuclear power generation", "Nuclear fuel cycle", "Nuclear plant maintenance and services", "Nuclear reactor design and construction", "Energy utilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Over 100,000 nuclear parts annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Technology powers 57% of world''s nuclear power plants", "Maintains nearly two-thirds of world''s nuclear fleet", "Fuels 40% of world''s nuclear fleet", "Supplies over 100,000 nuclear parts annually", "First commercial pressurized water reactor (1957)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1869 by George Westinghouse -> db, /about-us", "Headquarters Hopkins, South Carolina -> db", "Approximately 12,500 employees, 100+ locations, 23 countries -> /about-us", "Technology powers 57% of world''s nuclear plants, maintains nearly two-thirds of fleet, fuels 40% -> /", "Supplies over 100,000 nuclear parts annually -> db (products)", "First commercial pressurized water reactor in 1957 -> /about-us", "AP1000 Generation III+ reactor with passive safety -> /, /about-us", "Services: routine maintenance, emergent issues, integrated LMS, us