UPDATE companies SET description='White Bag Company, Inc. was founded in 1948 by Mr. White in Benton, Arkansas, where he collected used burlap bags from dairies, feed mills, and field workers while managing a Texaco service station.

The company operates as a wholesaler and distributor of paper, woven polypropylene, and FIBC bulk bags, sourcing inventory from overseas factories. It also runs an in-house four-color printing press for custom bag design and printing. Recent expansions added 10,000 square feet of warehouse space in 2022 and another 18,500 square feet in 2025, bringing significant covered storage and racking capacity.

White Bag serves agricultural and industrial packaging markets, with memberships in the Flexible Intermediate Bulk Container Association, the Southern Seed Association, and the Textile Bag and Packaging Association.

